The signalling messages follow Rubylight's WebRTC TV protocol, version 2
(https://github.com/RamazanKara/Rubylight) and the contract published in
Monlight-Tizen-WebRtc-Client (https://github.com/mlopezsegura/Monlight-Tizen-WebRtc-Client).

tizen/wasm/wake-on-lan.c is adapted from that client's tizen/wasm/wake-on-lan.c.

The authentication label moonlight-webrtc-tv-auth-v1 and the gamepad button
bits are part of that protocol. SHA-256 and HMAC-SHA256 in this tree are an
independent implementation of FIPS 180-4 and RFC 2104. A Tizen web app is not
a secure context, so crypto.subtle is not used.

The retired Windows gateway in tsoas/moonlight-webrtc-tizen is not included.

tizen/icon.png is a 512x512 raster of the Nightjar launcher mark in
RamazanKara/nightjar, file app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_nightjar_foreground.xml,
drawn on #14161F. That project is GPL-3.0.
